  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Audio Generation Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` simulates the core idea: train a tiny next-token transformer on synthetic \"audio token\" sequences generated from two distinct \"styles\" (alternating low and high tokens for style A, monotonic ramp for style B). Condition on style and sample."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: synthetic audio tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def make_tokens(style, length, vocab_size, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if style == 0:  # \"speech-like\": alternating"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [i % vocab_size for i in range(length)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    # \"music-like\": ramp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [(i * 3) % vocab_size for i in range(length)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: train a tiny token predictor"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A bigram-style predictor conditioned on style. The point is the pattern: codec tokens \u2192 cross-entropy training \u2192 autoregressive sampling."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: sample conditionally"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Given the style token and a starting token, sample the next token from the predicted distribution. Continue for 20-40 tokens."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py` and set style explicitly. Verify the generated sequences match the style's pattern.\n2. **Medium.** Add delayed parallel decoding: simulate 2 streams of tokens that must stay offset by 1 step. Train a joint predictor.\n3. **Hard.** Use HuggingFace transformers to run MusicGen-small locally. Generate a 10-second clip with three different prompts; A/B for style adherence."
      ]
    }
